# OpenEVV sound map: Chinese (Cantonese) (eSpeak NG voice sit/yue), spoken by openevv's German module
# with the sounds, the melody and the tones of the language itself.
# Written by engine/accent/mapwriter.py; OpenEvvFrontend reads it, and docs/LANGUAGES.md
# says what each line means. Edit freely: the file is read each time a voice starts.

template dedx
style standard
vowels i I e E a A u U o O y Y oe OE @ aj aw oj a~ E~ o~ oe~ E: R
glides j w
schwa @
secondary 2
words apart
onset 1
cluster k w
cluster g w

# the melody: tone; a question that wants yes or no: fall
accent f0=own range=100 level=30 decl=6 declmax=25 lag=70 lead=15 fs=-6 fq=6 qreg=18 fc=4 fe=0 fw=-4 span=1 stressed=88 weak=112 stop=1

# the tones, under eSpeak NG's names for them
tone 1 p=0:50,100:50
tone 7 p=0:50,100:32
tone 2 p=0:22,35:22,100:50 dur=108
tone 3 p=0:30,100:30
tone 4 p=0:22,100:10 creak=25 cfrom=60 cto=100
tone 5 p=0:20,35:20,100:32 dur=108
tone 6 p=0:22,100:21

# what the module says in place of a phone it is given
says C t S
says J d Z
says P p f
says T t s

# the sounds of the language that the module has not, each as it differs from the phone
# that stands for it: formants and lengths in per cent, times in milliseconds
